---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WikiCard from '../components/WikiCard.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../components/v2/templates/CategoryHub.astro';
import { siteImages } from '../data/images';
import { getPageSEO } from '../utils/seo';
const pageSEO = getPageSEO('equipment');
const cards = [
  { title: 'Stoves', description: 'Browse the stove category and its existing equipment entries.', href: '/equipment/stoves/', icon: 'S' },
  { title: 'Chiller', description: 'Open the current limited Wiki entry for the Chiller.', href: '/equipment/chiller/', icon: 'C' },
];
---
<BaseLayout pageId="equipment" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: pageSEO.h1 }]}>
  <CategoryHub title={pageSEO.h1} kicker="Restaurant tools" intro="Browse restaurant equipment and learn how each category supports the service workflow." cards={cards} relatedLinks={[{ label: 'Beginner Guide', href: '/guides/beginner-guide/', description: 'Learn how equipment connects with the complete restaurant service loop.' }, { label: 'Cooking and Serving Guide', href: '/guides/cooking-and-serving/', description: 'See where cooking equipment fits into an order from preparation to serving.' }, { label: 'Upgrade Priority Guide', href: '/guides/upgrade-priority/', description: 'Choose changes that address the restaurant area currently needing attention.' }, { label: 'Counter Upgrades', href: '/guides/counter-upgrades/', description: 'Review counter changes as a separate restaurant improvement.' }]} heroImage={siteImages.equipmentHero} tableOfContents browseHeading="Equipment Directory" copyHeading="Introduction" relatedHeading="Related Guides" adSlots>
  <p>Equipment includes the restaurant tools and work areas used during daily service. This hub organizes the equipment categories currently covered by the Wiki and connects them with guides that explain the wider cooking and restaurant workflow.</p>

  <h2 id="how-equipment-works">How Equipment Works</h2>
  <p>Restaurant equipment is organized by the part of the restaurant where each entry belongs. Stoves form the documented cooking-equipment directory. The Chiller remains a separate named entry, but its detailed function is not asserted by this hub.</p>
  <p>Equipment works alongside ingredients, customer orders, furniture, and player movement. An equipment change is most useful when it addresses a problem in the part of the restaurant where that tool is used. The <a href="/guides/cooking-and-serving/">Cooking and Serving Guide</a> shows how cooking equipment connects with the complete order workflow.</p>

  <h2 id="featured-content">Featured Content</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <WikiCard title="Stoves" description="Browse the cooking-equipment category and its existing articles." href="/equipment/stoves/" icon="S" />
    <WikiCard title="Chiller" description="Read the current limited Wiki entry without assuming unconfirmed functions." href="/equipment/chiller/" icon="C" />
    <WikiCard title="Cooking and Serving" description="Follow an order through preparation, cooking, and customer service." href="/guides/cooking-and-serving/" icon="G" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="choosing-equipment">Choosing Equipment</h2>
  <p>Start with the task you are trying to understand, then open the matching equipment entry. For cooking-related questions, begin with the Stove directory. Use the other category hubs when the question is really about ingredients, furniture placement, or task organization.</p>
  <p>Choose equipment for the job it supports rather than following a fixed purchase order. After changing the restaurant setup, follow several customer orders from start to finish and check whether the original problem is easier to manage.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Keep movement paths around equipment clear during restaurant service.</li>
    <li>Place frequently used work areas where they fit naturally into the order workflow.</li>
    <li>Check ingredient supplies and restaurant organization before assuming equipment is the problem.</li>
    <li>Change one part of the setup at a time so its effect on the workflow is easier to understand.</li>
    <li>Use the directory to read about an equipment category without assuming properties that are not shown in the game.</li>
  </ul>
  </CategoryHub>
</BaseLayout>
